<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#antipattern/binover/refactoring-1> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[Mod] Fix stereotype:" ;
    skos:definition "[Mod] Fix stereotype: change the stereotype of the relation to fit a desired binary property" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/BinOver/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 1 ;
    ok:sourceText "**[Mod] Fix stereotype:** change the stereotype of the relation to fit a desired binary property" .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#antipattern/binover/refactoring-2> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[OCL] Enforce binary property:" ;
    skos:definition "[OCL] Enforce binary property: create OCL invariant to enforce a desired binary property (as long as it is compatible with the embedded constraints of the stereotype)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/BinOver/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 2 ;
    ok:sourceText "**[OCL] Enforce binary property:** create OCL invariant to enforce a desired binary property (as long as it is compatible with the embedded constraints of the stereotype)." .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#antipattern/binover/refactoring-3> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[New] Enforce disjointness:" ;
    skos:definition "[New] Enforce disjointness: make the related types disjoint by the specification of a disjoint generalization set." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/BinOver/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:sourceText "**[New] Enforce disjointness:** make the related types disjoint by the specification of a disjoint generalization set." .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#antipattern/decint/refactoring-1> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[conditional] [Mod] Fix Generalization Set:" ;
    skos:definition "[conditional] [Mod] Fix Generalization Set: can only be adopted if two or more parent types are made disjoint by a generalization set. The possible solutions are to remove the existing generalization set or set its isCovering property to true." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/DecInt/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 1 ;
    ok:sourceText "**[conditional] [Mod] Fix Generalization Set:** can only be adopted if two or more parent types are made disjoint by a generalization set. The possible solutions are to remove the existing generalization set or set its isCovering property to true." .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#antipattern/decint/refactoring-2> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[conditional] [Mod] Fix Identity Principle:" ;
    skos:definition "[conditional] [Mod] Fix Identity Principle: can only be applied if Type is sortal («Subkind», «Role» or «Phase») and they do not follow the same identity principle. The action consists on defining the single identity provider." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/DecInt/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 2 ;
    ok:references ontouml:phase,
        ontouml:role,
        ontouml:subkind ;
    ok:sourceText "**[conditional] [Mod] Fix Identity Principle:** can only be applied if Type is sortal («:ref:`Subkind`», «:ref:`Role`» or «:ref:`Phase`») and they do not follow the same identity principle. The action consists on defining the single identity provider." .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#antipattern/decint/refactoring-3> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[Mod/Del] Invert/Delete Generalization:" ;
    skos:definition "[Mod/Del] Invert/Delete Generalization: consists of deleting and/or inverting one or more generalizations from Type to one of the identified parents." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/DecInt/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:sourceText "**[Mod/Del] Invert/Delete Generalization:** consists of deleting and/or inverting one or more generalizations from Type to one of the identified parents." .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#antipattern/decint/refactoring-4> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[OCL] Derived by Intersection:" ;
    skos:definition """[OCL] Derived by Intersection: create an OCL derivation or invariant constraint to specify that the extension of type is derived by the intersection of the extensions of two or more concrete parents:
 | context Parent1
 | inv: (self.oclIsTypeOf(Parent2) and self.oclIsTypeOf(Parent2))
 | implies self.oclIsTypeOf(Type)""" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/DecInt/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 4 ;
    ok:sourceText """**[OCL] Derived by Intersection:** create an OCL derivation or invariant constraint to specify that the extension of type is derived by the intersection of the extensions of two or more concrete parents:

			| *context Parent1*
			| *inv: (self.oclIsTypeOf(Parent2) and self.oclIsTypeOf(Parent2))*
			| *implies self.oclIsTypeOf(Type)*""" .

